OL,3,GNEWSAWhat is being done to stop        
OL,4,Adisruptive cable theft?                
OL,6,FThe theft of copper cables can wipe out
OL,7,Ftelecommunications and plunge homes,   
OL,8,Fbusinesses and transport networks into 
OL,9,Fa digital blackout - as seen during a  
OL,10,Frecent spate in Bedfordshire.          
OL,12,FWith the scrap value of the metal wires
OL,13,Fattracting criminal gangs, what is     
OL,14,Fbeing done to prevent damage to the    
OL,15,Fnetwork and all the disruption it      
OL,16,Fcauses?                                
OL,18,FIn the early hours of 12 November,     
OL,19,Fabout a mile (1.6km) of underground    
OL,20,Fcable was stolen beside an A-road in   
OL,21,FWilstead, near Bedford.                
OL,23,APub: 21-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
